  "evidence_basis": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "F01_M0_ACTIONS",
      "source_type": "M0",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY01/m0.md",
      "source_sha256": "4cce89f12f278559f45ac0d3bbb6dae049e72dc059866bb1fb039ab74aaa5a0a",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 14,
        "end_line": 19,
        "excerpt_sha256": "9d463b8aa018771d74f30d5e42cec103419c00ba5a65277c61e10f92147d3f0b"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "- ROUTINE_MONITORING: no additional thermal-triggered check.\n- SOIL_MOISTURE_CONFIRMATION: send a technician to measure volumetric water content (VWC) at the fixed root-zone probe.\n- REPEAT_THERMAL_SCAN: collect a second scan after checking camera and air-sensor setup.\n- INPUT_INVALID: stop when required calibration, time, geometry, or sensor-quality fields are absent.\n\nThermal output only prioritizes confirmation. A separate site agronomist applies the site's irrigation rule to the soil probe and plant-water evidence.\n",
      "supports": "Names the frozen M0 triage actions that this candidate keeps available.",
      "claim_type": "method_rule"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "F01_M0_SELECTION",
      "source_type": "M0",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY01/m0.md",
      "source_sha256": "4cce89f12f278559f45ac0d3bbb6dae049e72dc059866bb1fb039ab74aaa5a0a",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 21,
        "end_line": 27,
        "excerpt_sha256": "471e308b6e8c857a5c00f91b75f5cb652ed4a9c9244e596e1a4be92770fe8516"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "## Selection procedure\n\n1. Confirm the radiometric camera's blackbody check is within ±0.2 °C; verify the paired shielded air sensor, camera time, plot, scan geometry, and canopy mask.\n2. For each scan, calculate D = median masked canopy temperature − matched air temperature.\n3. Take two scans ten minutes apart from the same marked block. If setup or mask quality fails, use INPUT_INVALID. If the pair differs by more than 0.8 °C, use REPEAT_THERMAL_SCAN.\n4. If both D values are at least 2.0 °C, select SOIL_MOISTURE_CONFIRMATION. If both are below 2.0 °C, select ROUTINE_MONITORING. If the pair straddles 2.0 °C, select REPEAT_THERMAL_SCAN.\n5. Under the independent site protocol, VWC below 16% triggers an agronomist review; VWC at or above 16% leaves the block in routine monitoring unless separate plant-water evidence warrants review. Do not infer irrigation from D alone.\n",
      "supports": "Defines M0 setup validity, paired scans, thresholds, and separate VWC review; used only for baseline and stop context.",
      "claim_type": "method_rule"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "F01_E1_TRIGGER",
      "source_type": "E1",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY01/revision-evidence-e1.md",
      "source_sha256": "8c4d4123055732d8e68a13eaa0dcb9fbae3cddb07afef66e7dbb3699ea761ca0",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 14,
        "end_line": 15,
        "excerpt_sha256": "a2ba640a77fdfd6331416956aeba5508130a4227cf57abb83fa8043f787f83a6"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "| OBS-01 | reflective silver film, measured reflectance 0.72; bearing toward sun at 21° off nadir | 2.7 / 2.6 | 23.0% | water potential −0.55 MPa; no wilt | canopy radiance estimate exceeded contact reference by 1.6 °C |\n| OBS-02 | same silver-film block, repeat 12 min later, same bearing | 2.6 / 2.5 | 22.7% | water potential −0.52 MPa; no wilt | excess over contact reference 1.5 °C |\n",
      "supports": "Two observed silver-film records triggered M0 while contact-reference excess and independent water observations did not indicate dry soil.",
      "claim_type": "observed"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "F01_E1_CONTROLS",
      "source_type": "E1",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY01/revision-evidence-e1.md",
      "source_sha256": "8c4d4123055732d8e68a13eaa0dcb9fbae3cddb07afef66e7dbb3699ea761ca0",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 16,
        "end_line": 18,
        "excerpt_sha256": "bae5e8bcd9e23d5f0938b36e8dc3a2f624854c66e70fe3f94d7582688df8868a"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "| OBS-03 | same marked canopy and film; bearing rotated away from sun to 8° off nadir | 1.0 / 0.9 | 22.9% | water potential −0.54 MPa; no wilt | excess over contact reference 0.2 °C |\n| OBS-04 | ordinary mineral soil, reflectance 0.14; toward-sun bearing at 21° off nadir; matched weather | 0.9 / 0.8 | 22.4% | water potential −0.56 MPa; no wilt | excess over contact reference 0.1 °C |\n| OBS-05 | ordinary mineral soil, reflectance 0.15; same bearing and camera | 2.5 / 2.4 | 11.8% | water potential −1.62 MPa; visible wilt | excess over contact reference 0.2 °C |\n",
      "supports": "The changed bearing, ordinary-surface comparison, and positive control bound the observed contrast.",
      "claim_type": "observed"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "F01_E1_LIMITS",
      "source_type": "E1",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY01/revision-evidence-e1.md",
      "source_sha256": "8c4d4123055732d8e68a13eaa0dcb9fbae3cddb07afef66e7dbb3699ea761ca0",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 25,
        "end_line": 27,
        "excerpt_sha256": "bd704ec4eac53b5454f80aa1129f814331adb750a8137bb172c53a7dd3ff0ecf"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "OBS-01 and OBS-02 satisfy M0's repeated thermal trigger while independent VWC and plant-water observations do not indicate dry soil. OBS-03 changes the bearing for the same canopy and does not reproduce the excess seen in OBS-01/OBS-02. OBS-04 is a low-reflectance, matched-bearing comparison. OBS-05 is a positive control in which M0's trigger and independent water indicators agree. OBS-06 has incomplete surface coverage and variable paired readings; it does not isolate one stable measurement context.\n\nThe packet supports investigating a measurement-boundary defect associated with the observed surface/radiance/view combination. It does not establish a universal reflectance cutoff, a corrected thermal threshold, or an action for every reflective surface. Weather, canopy masking, the ordinary-surface positive control, and instrument calibration remain plausible checks; the records above do not support discarding all thermal measurements or moving M0's global 2.0 °C criterion.\n",
      "supports": "Supports investigating only the observed surface/radiance/view combination and explicitly rejects universal cutoffs or a global M0 threshold change.",
      "claim_type": "method_rule"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "F01_E1_QUALITY",
      "source_type": "E1",
      "source_path": "ignition/reports/evaluations/ignition-220-cognitive-evolution-r0/families/FAMILY01/revision-evidence-e1.md",
      "source_sha256": "8c4d4123055732d8e68a13eaa0dcb9fbae3cddb07afef66e7dbb3699ea761ca0",
      "locator": {
        "start_line": 21,
        "end_line": 21,
        "excerpt_sha256": "6c4673b7783efe4c6b2ad5f64e3bf3d7d8a09acbe40b1242379b0ebd62bbc9f6"
      },
      "display_excerpt": "All six records passed camera/air-sensor quality checks and were within M0 ambient-temperature and canopy-height limits. The site VWC review threshold was 16%. Raw values are also present in F01-E1-CAMPAIGN-LOG rows keyed by the locators above.\n",
      "supports": "The named E1 records passed the stated camera and air-sensor quality checks.",
      "claim_type": "observed"
    }
  ],
